==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*hugjaną||think, consider}}. Cognate with Gothic [[𐌷𐌿𐌲𐌾𐌰𐌽]], Old Norse [[huga]] (Icelandic [[hugsa]] ‘to think’). Related to Middle Scots [[huik]] ‘regard, consider’.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhyd.d͡ʒɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|head=hyċġan}}

# to [[think]]
# to think about, to [[consider]]

